# Repo hygiene

## Package manager: pnpm only

- Use **pnpm** everywhere (`pnpm install`, `pnpm add`, `pnpm exec`). Never run `npm install`, `npm ci`, or `yarn`.
- Lockfiles: commit **`pnpm-lock.yaml`** only. Never commit or leave behind `package-lock.json` or `yarn.lock`.
- Root and `mobile/` both pin **`pnpm@11.5.0`** via `packageManager` in each `package.json`.
- After dependency changes, run `pnpm install` in the affected package and commit the updated lockfile.

## Delete stray artifacts when you see them

Remove and do not commit:

| Artifact | Why |
|----------|-----|
| `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock` | Wrong package manager |
| `node_modules/`, `.pnpm-store/` | Install output |
| `dist/`, `build/`, `coverage/` | Build/test output |
| `*.tsbuildinfo`, `test-results/`, `playwright-report/` | Tooling output |
| Duplicate files (e.g. `Foo.tsx` + `foo.tsx`) | Windows casing drift |

## When cleaning up

- If `package-lock.json` appears after someone used npm, delete it and regenerate with `pnpm install`.
- Prefer one canonical filename per module (**`filenames.mdc`** — kebab-case under `src/` and `mobile/src/`).
- Do not add npm/yarn scripts or CI steps; mobile CI already uses pnpm.
